<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">10 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 10 October, from 415 to 1967.</p></header>
<div class="tih-pinned-card"><p class="tih-pinned-label">International day</p><p class="tih-pinned-title">World Mental Health Day</p><p class="tih-pinned-desc">Observed since 1992 under the World Federation for Mental Health and endorsed by the World Health Organisation, World Mental Health Day promotes global awareness of mental health issues and advocates for open discussion and improved access to care.</p></div>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/theodosius-ii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theodosius-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">415 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,611 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Theodosius II inaugurates the second church of Hagia Sophia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodosius-ii">Theodosius II</a> inaugurated the church he had commissioned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, the second on the site of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia</a>. A fifth-century list of monuments named it the Great Church; the present building, the last of three, was completed in 537.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/680">680 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,346 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Husayn ibn Ali is killed at the Battle of Karbala</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/husayn-ibn-ali">Husayn ibn Ali</a>, grandson of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prophet-muhammad">Prophet Muhammad</a>, who had refused to recognise the Umayyad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazid-i">Yazid I</a>, was killed with most of his small band by Yazid's forces at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-karbala">Karbala</a>. His death became central to Shia identity.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-karbala">Battle of Karbala</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/husayn-ibn-ali">Husayn ibn Ali</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazid-i">Yazid I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/732">732 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,294 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles Martel defeats an Umayyad army near Tours</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Frankish forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-martel">Charles Martel</a> defeated an Arab and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> army led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-al-ghafiqi">Abd al-Rahman al-Ghafiqi</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tours">Tours</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poitiers">Poitiers</a>; the traditional date is 10 October. How decisive the battle was remains debated.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-martel">Charles Martel</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1471">1471 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">555 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sten Sture the Elder defeats Christian I at Brunkeberg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On a ridge outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stockholm">Stockholm</a>, the Swedish regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sten-sture-the-elder">Sten Sture the Elder</a>, with peasants, miners and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burghers">burghers</a>, defeated King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christian-i-of-denmark">Christian I of Denmark</a>, who sought to enforce his rule over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalmar-union">Kalmar Union</a>. The victory secured Sture's regency.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-brunkeberg">Battle of Brunkeberg</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sten-sture-the-elder">Sten Sture the Elder</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christian-i-of-denmark">Christian I of Denmark</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1760">1760 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">266 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Ndyuka Maroons win autonomy by treaty with the Dutch</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndyuka">Ndyuka</a>, a Maroon people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a> descended from Africans who escaped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>, signed a treaty with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> colonial authorities recognising their territorial autonomy. In 2010 Suriname made 10 October a national holiday, the Day of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maroons">Maroons</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maroons">Maroons</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1845">1845 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">181 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The US Naval School opens at Annapolis</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Naval School, renamed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Naval Academy in 1850, opened at Fort Severn in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/annapolis-maryland">Annapolis, Maryland</a>, with 50 midshipmen. It has trained American naval officers ever since; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jimmy-carter">Jimmy Carter</a> was among its graduates.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1911">1911 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">115 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Wuchang Uprising sparks the Chinese revolution</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Revolutionary soldiers mutinied at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wuchang">Wuchang</a>, beginning the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinhai-revolution">Xinhai Revolution</a>. Within months the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing dynasty</a> abdicated, ending more than two thousand years of imperial rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinhai-revolution">Xinhai Revolution</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wuchang">Wuchang</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1913">1913 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">113 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Woodrow Wilson triggers the blast that floods the Panama Canal cut</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">From the White House, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/woodrow-wilson">President Wilson</a> sent a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telegraph">telegraph</a> signal that detonated the Gamboa dike. Water flowed into the Culebra Cut, joining the canal's waters ten months before it opened to shipping.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/woodrow-wilson">Woodrow Wilson</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1967">1967 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">59 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Outer Space Treaty enters into force</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Outer Space Treaty came into effect, forming the basis of international space law. It bars nuclear weapons from orbit and forbids any nation from claiming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhu">Moon</a> or other celestial bodies.</p></div></li></ol>
